// @emit-error field access but no struct type declared
// A FLOOR PIN, not a decision — flip it when the floor lifts, and read the axis below first.
// A verdict pin rather than a `@log` one because there is no correct output to observe: the
// program never lowers, so the only thing this file can hold still is WHICH message it takes
// and WHICH cell takes it.
//
// AN UN-ANNOTATED binding whose object literal's field-name SET equals a union VARIANT's.
// `collectAnonShapes` skips such a literal (`objVariantName(ai) != ""`, on the reading that
// it will be boxed as an arm), and a variant's own `TypeDecl` is deliberately absent from the
// struct table (`collectS` skips `variantIndexOf(…) >= 0` — the variant table owns it). So
// the literal gets no layout from either table and the read has no receiver.
//
// THE AXIS IS THE FIELDSET TWIN PLUS THE MISSING ANNOTATION. IT IS NOT ABOUT STRUCT-TYPED
// FIELDS, AND THE DEPTH-1 i32 SHAPE IN THIS FILE IS THE PROOF: `{p: i32}` has no struct-typed
// field, no nesting, and one field. It was filed as "the union-variant field collector's
// restriction leaking onto a binding that is not in the union", and it is not — the collector
// fix that lifted `variant-inline-shape-field.vl` moved this cell zero, message for message.
//
// MEASURED, each cell its own program:
//   - annotate the binding `: Outer` and the message CHANGES to `ref valtype with no interned
//     shape` — a second, separate floor (`variant-annotated-global-floor.vl`);
//   - make it a LOCAL instead of a global and this same message stands (storage class is not
//     the axis for the un-annotated cell, though it IS for the annotated one);
//   - give the literal a field set no variant shares (`{k: 5}`) and it lowers;
//   - drop the union and it lowers;
//   - a DEEPER shape does not change the root, only which wrong struct it collides with: with
//     `Inner = {v: i32}` beside `Outer = {v: Inner}` the same program reports `nested struct
//     fields are not supported`, because the orphan literal then matches `Inner`'s field set
//     and is lowered against `Inner`'s layout. That message is a downstream artifact of the
//     collision, not evidence about field types.
//
// THE GUARD IS LOAD-BEARING AND THAT WAS MEASURED TOO. Deleting `&& objVariantName(ai) == ""`
// lowers this file and every cell of its grid, and reddens 7 of 1,524 `@run` corpus rows —
// among them `types/variant-as-value.vl`, which PINS a variant type as a first-class value.
// Minting an `#anon` row for a variant-twinned literal makes later same-fieldset literals
// resolve to that row instead of the variant, so variant CONSTRUCTION breaks. The repair has
// to give the anon pass the literal's context, which it does not have; a blunt relaxation is
// a regression with a pin already standing against it.
type Outer = { p: i32 }
type U = Outer | i32

const g = { p: 5 }
print(g.p)
